Ready for a job full of action? Come work at Wasco in Deventer! As a warehouse worker, you’ll work in various departments. Stay active and earn up to €24,32 per hour.

For this function you will need your own housing in the Netherlands. Unfortunately we do not offer housing with this job. Apply now and get a WhatsApp message within 15 minutes with questions so we can help you quickly. Do not have a WhatsApp? Then we will contact you by phone or email!

What we offer
- Amazing salary starting at €16,21 per hour
- Travel expenses? Covered!
- Earn up to €24,32 per hour including bonuses
- Every weekend off! Yes, you read that right!
- Full-time? Part-time? YES!
- Fun activities & sing-along to the best hits

Who you are
To keep the Wasco warehouse running smoothly, it is important that you meet the following requirements as a warehouse worker:

-     You speak English, for safety reasons;    
- You are at least 18 years old, due to driving an EPT;    
- You are at least available to work on Mondays and Fridays (more days are possible);    
- You are available to work in different shifts. The working hours are from 09:00 to 18:00,    12:00 to 21:00 and 15:00 to 00.00;    
- You have your own transport to get to Deventer;    
- You are physically capable of lifting product weighing at least 20 kilos;    
- You agree that we can not offer a guarantee of hours.

What will you do
As a warehouse worker at Wasco in Deventer, no two days are the same. You can work in various departments, depending on what suits you best. For example, you might work in the receiving department. This is where you greet drivers, check deliveries, and handle the administrative paperwork. In the modern “autostore,” you’ll work with smart systems and pick small parts like screws and connectors. Prefer a more hands-on role? Then the order picker position is a good fit for you. You’ll pick larger products like bathtubs and radiators. As a warehouse worker, you’ll work Monday through Friday. If you’d prefer to work fewer

In this position, you will be responsible for assembling, connecting, and maintaining industrial electrical systems. You will work with power distribution systems, cable routes, control panels, and industrial machinery. Together with your team, you ensure that installations operate safely and efficiently.

Your tasks include:

- Installing and connecting industrial electrical equipment;
- Reading electrical diagrams and technical documentation;
- Troubleshooting and repairing electrical malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations and carrying out maintenance work;
- Working together with colleagues and supervisors on-site.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering;
- Experience in industrial electrical work;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain it;
- Knowledge of NEN 1010 and NEN 3140 is a plus;
- Independent and accurate working attitude;
- Dutch or English speaking.

Are you looking for a dynamic position in manufacturing that involves physical labor and operating a forklift? Do you enjoy working shifts and do you like variety? Then this is your chance!

We’re looking for a forklift operator/production worker for the 5-shift system at a leading animal feed manufacturer in Ittervoort. In this role, you’ll be responsible for mixing meat with other raw materials and ingredients to create the correct composition for the final product. You’ll work with a mixing system and a forklift.

What will you be doing?

- Operating a forklift to transport and move raw materials;
- Operating mixing equipment to create the correct mixtures;
- Ensuring a clean and safe work environment;
- Recording production data;
- Identifying and reporting deviations in the process.

You’ll work in 5 shifts, with the following work hours: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. You’ll work 8.5 hours a day and be paid for 8 hours. You’ll work 6 days in a row and then have 4 days off. To ensure you’re properly trained, you may start in the day shift. 

- You have a valid forklift operator's license and proven experience;
- You speak Dutch or English; 
- You are available full-time for the 5-shift schedule.

As an Electrical & Instrumentation Technician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial environments. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, electrical panels, and automated installations that are essential for reliable production processes.

Your daily activities include:

- Installing, maintaining, and repairing electrical and instrumentation systems;
- Calibrating, testing, and commissioning instrumentation equipment;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing inspections and preventive maintenance activities;
- Ensuring compliance with safety regulations, including ATEX requirements;
- Supporting production and engineering teams with technical expertise.

Depending on the project, you may work at industrial production sites, processing plants, or workshop facilities.

- Completed MBO level 3 or 4 education in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, or a related technical discipline;
- Relevant experience within industrial electrical engineering or E&I environments;
- Knowledge of NEN standards and ATEX regulations is preferred;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driver’s license B;
- Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
- Good command of the Dutch and/or English language

Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.
